; Fixture for recurring-subscription detection (reports::subscriptions).
;
; Scanned with as_of = 2026-06-30 and a 24-month lookback (window opens
; 2024-06-30). Every payee below exists to pin one behaviour of the detector:
;
;   Netflix       18 × $15.99 on the 15th          -> MONTHLY (the easy case)
;   Spotify       12 × $10.99 rising to $11.99     -> MONTHLY (price rise inside tolerance)
;   Apple         15 × $9.99 on the 20th, PLUS     -> MONTHLY, $9.99 only
;                 4 one-off app purchases             (the mixed-payee case)
;   Amazon        11 × wildly varying amounts      -> NOT a subscription
;   Hover         2  × $35.00 every September      -> ANNUAL
;   State Farm    2  × $1,200 every November       -> ANNUAL (2-day drift)
;   Gold's Gym    4  × $45.00 on the 5th           -> NOT a subscription (below min_monthly)
;   City Water    6  × $60.00 every 3 months       -> NOT monthly (quarterly must not qualify)
;   Acme Corp     6  × payroll tax withholding     -> NOT a subscription (income guard)
;   Safeway       7  × varying, 2 a year apart     -> NOT annual (coincidental pair)
;   Wells Fargo   8  × $2,400 on the 1st           -> NOT a subscription (excluded by description)
;   Hulu          6  × $12.99, stopped Jun 2025    -> CANCELLED (card is current, so silence is real)
;   Backblaze     6  × $9.00, stopped Sep 2025     -> KEPT (its bank account's import stops there too)
;   Twilio        5  × wildly varying, 2 tagged    -> MONTHLY via subscription:true (one entry, deduped)
;   Dropbox       6  × $11.99, one tagged false    -> SUPPRESSED via subscription:false
;
; Deliberately NOT balanced against real bank history — every charge is funded
; from a single credit-card account, which is all the detector looks at.

account expenses:subscriptions
account expenses:shopping
account expenses:utilities
account expenses:housing
account liabilities:creditcard
account assets:oldbank:checking

